mpare source and stored byte counts and SHA-256 before reporting custody. Record source-run provenance separately: matching current files and attachments does not prove an older capture came from a particular build or revision. Inspect the installed schemas and use normal registered lifecycle calls; stage local files rather than copying printed base64. For visual changes require the worker's actual screenshots/recording and self-contained HTML report. Inspect the visible state of each capture and compare hashes for supposedly distinct states: matching files or an unrelated error screen cannot prove the states named by their filenames. Hold visual acceptance and request only the missing real captures. Inspect evidence privately and relay requested or genuinely necessary final files through Hermes MEDIA to the originating chat/topic; do not dump intermediate proof packages into the chat. A drawing explains a concept; it cannot prove that an app worked. Record accepted delivery evidence before closing the ledger item. Failed or inaccessible artifacts leave that output unfinished.
